    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute low back strain (S39.012A)</content>. Mechanical right lower back pain after lifting, reproduced by movement and paraspinal pressure, without red flags for fracture, infection, cancer, or nerve compression. New back pain in a patient with an aneurysm must first be weighed as possible aneurysm pain: here the aneurysm is non-tender, his blood pressure and pulse are stable, he has no fainting or abdominal pain, and the same-day duplex ultrasound shows no change in size and no fluid around the aorta. A symptomatic aneurysm is therefore not suspected, and no CT is needed today. [S]<list><item>Stay active, with short walks; avoid heavy lifting and twisting for two weeks.</item><item>Heat to the back; acetaminophen 1 g up to three times a day as needed, no more than 3 g a day.</item><item>Avoid ibuprofen, naproxen, and other anti-inflammatory pain medicines, which add bleeding risk to aspirin and can harm the kidneys with losartan; avoid muscle relaxants, which cause drowsiness and falls at his age.</item><item>Expect improvement within one to two weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Infrarenal abdominal aortic aneurysm under surveillance (I71.43)</content>. Diameter unchanged at 5.0 cm by duplex ultrasound. The emergency plan was reviewed and he followed it correctly today. [S]<list><item>Call emergency services at once for sudden or severe abdominal, back, flank, or groin pain, pain that changes in character, fainting, or a tender pulsating lump.</item><item>Keep the next surveillance scan at six months, as planned.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: The Society for Vascular Surgery practice guidelines on the care of patients with an abdominal aortic aneurysm (2018); 2022 ACC/AHA Guideline for the Diagnosis and Management of Aortic Disease (2022); Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check in three days. Return the same day if the pain changes, spreads, or comes with any of the emergency signs. Three-month review as planned in six weeks. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-14: three-month review: blood pressure, lipids on a statin, and smoking cessation. [S]</paragraph></text>

